## Data Persistence Layer (`store.js`)

All persistent data is stored in a single in-memory object `_store`, keyed by filename. On startup, `loadAllData()` reads all eight JSON files from disk (Tauri) or from `localStorage` (browser) and populates `_store`. All subsequent reads are synchronous via `getData(filename)`. Writes call `saveData(filename, data)` which updates `_store` immediately and then fires an async `invoke('write_data_file', ...)` in the background — writes never block the UI.

On first launch after upgrading from an older build, `loadAllData()` migrates legacy `localStorage` keys (`ny_bookmarks`, `ny_progress`, etc.) to their corresponding JSON files and removes the old keys.

The MU metadata cache (`muCache`) is loaded separately by `_initMuCache()`, which runs immediately after `loadAllData()`. It evicts entries older than 30 days and entries that predate the `status` field addition before assigning the result to the `muCache` variable.

