## Reader

### Chapter loading

`openLocalChapter(idx)` clears the current chapter via `freePages()`, determines the page source (Tauri native, PDF, or FSAPI), builds `reader.pages`, resolves the start page from saved progress, preloads the first four pages via `preloadLocal()`, runs `applyAutoLayout()` to detect webtoon format, then renders.

### Page sources

- **Tauri image chapters** — `convertFileSrc(path)` transforms disk paths to asset protocol URLs. These are assigned at chapter-open time. No IPC or blob creation per page.
- **PDF chapters (Tauri)** — `pdfjsLib.getDocument(assetUrl)` opens the document. Pages are rendered on demand in `preloadPdfPage()`: `pdfDoc.getPage(n)` → `pdfPage.render()` to an off-screen canvas → `canvas.toBlob()` → `URL.createObjectURL()`. Render height is fixed at 1200px.
- **FSAPI image chapters** — `FileHandle.getFile()` → `URL.createObjectURL()`. Blob URLs are revoked when the chapter closes.

### Memory management

`freePages()` iterates `reader.pages`, revokes all blob URLs where `revoke: true`, and calls `pdfDoc.destroy()` on each unique PDF document object (deduplicated via `Set`). This runs at chapter-open and when navigating away from the reader.

`_evictPdfPages(curIdx)` is called on every page turn and strip scroll update. It revokes blob URLs for rendered PDF pages more than 2 positions from `curIdx` and resets their `url` to null so they can be re-rendered if revisited. This keeps a maximum of 5 decoded PDF page bitmaps in memory simultaneously.

### Long strip mode

`renderStrip()` creates DOM nodes for all pages but only sets `img.src` immediately for pages within ±5 of `curPage`. All other pages are registered with an `IntersectionObserver` (`rootMargin: 200% 0px`) that fires `preloadLocal()` as they scroll into proximity. The observer is stored in `_stripObserver` and disconnected in `_disconnectStripScroll()` on every navigation or re-render.

A `rAF`-throttled scroll listener keeps `reader.curPage` in sync with the visible page and calls `_evictPdfPages` on each update.

### Preload buffer sizes

| Mode | Pages ahead | Pages behind |
|------|-------------|--------------|
| Long strip | ±5 from curPage (IntersectionObserver) | — |
| Single page | 4 | 2 |
| Spread | 4 | 2 |

### Auto-layout detection

`detectLongStrip()` samples up to three already-loaded pages, measures their natural `height / width` ratio via `Image()`, and returns true if the average exceeds 2.5. Standard manga pages run 1.3–1.8; webtoon strips are typically 3–20. The result is applied per-chapter without overwriting the user's saved layout preference.

