## Rust Command Surface

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `read_dir` | Returns directory entries with name, path, is_dir |
| `set_library_root` | Sets the validated library root in Rust state |
| `clear_library_root` | Clears Rust-side library root on library change |
| `load_library_path` | Reads legacy library path from file (migration) |
| `get_series_size` | Recursively sums folder size in bytes |
| `count_pdf_pages` | Returns page count for a PDF file |
| `pick_folder` | Opens a native folder picker dialog |
| `pick_image_file` | Opens a native image file picker |
| `start_library_watcher` | Begins watching the library root; fires `library-changed` events |
| `cache_cover` | Downloads a cover URL to the app cache dir; returns the local path |
| `cache_custom_cover` | Copies a local image file to the cover cache |
| `delete_cached_cover` | Removes a cached cover by series ID |
| `open_folder_path` | Opens a folder in the system file explorer |
| `open_url` | Opens a URL in the system default browser |
| `search_mu` | Proxies a MangaUpdates search POST request |
| `fetch_mu_series` | Proxies a MangaUpdates series GET request |
| `get_app_version` | Returns the version from Cargo.toml at runtime |
| `check_for_updates` | Queries the GitHub releases API and returns update metadata |
| `download_and_install_update` | Downloads a platform installer and launches it |
| `move_to_trash_folder` | Moves a series directory into `[library]/_trash` after path validation |

The `search_mu` and `fetch_mu_series` commands exist because the MangaUpdates API does not send CORS headers that allow direct browser requests. All network calls to `api.mangaupdates.com` are proxied through Rust using `reqwest`.

