## Known Constraints

**No ES modules.** All code shares a single global scope. Function and variable names must be unique across all files. This is a deliberate trade-off to avoid a build step.

**No browser PDF cover caching.** `cache_cover` and `cache_custom_cover` are Tauri-only commands. In browser mode, cover images are fetched directly from MangaUpdates URLs with no local caching.

**FSAPI limitations.** In browser mode, directory handles must be re-requested on each session — the app cannot auto-reopen the library. There is no size computation, no file watcher, and no update checking. Multi-select and trash are disabled since `move_to_trash_folder` is Tauri-only.

**MU search quality.** The automatic match selects the first result whose title exactly matches the folder name (case-insensitive), falling back to the top result. Series with names that differ significantly from their MangaUpdates titles will match incorrectly and require a manual override via the identify modal.

**PDF.js memory floor.** Each rendered PDF page is a JPEG blob created from a canvas. The minimum practical memory for a PDF chapter is approximately 5 decoded pages at 45 MB per page at 1200px render height. This is a PDF.js architectural constraint, not an application one.

**Single-window only.** There is no multi-window support. Opening a second chapter always replaces the current reader state.
